; A document arranged around a file it does NOT carry — the shape
; `tempura inline` exists for.
;
; The anchor names the corpus's `skeleton-smf` fixture by a relative
; path, because plan 02 resolves an `:file` "relative to the document"
; and this document lives in `src/cli/testdata/`. `:size` and `:sha256`
; are that file's own: a by-reference anchor that declares neither is
; `anchor_mismatch` the moment a resolver reads it, and they are what
; makes an offset meaningful against this exact file (it 03's rule).
;
; They are also the reason this file is reviewed beside the corpus: the
; fixture is regenerated by `zig build fixtures` and hash-pinned by
; `corpus/skeleton-smf/expected.sjon`, so a drift fails there and here at
; once and both diffs are read together (the policy `tools/cli_golden.sh`
; states for every fixture it borrows).
;
; The comment above the note and the blank lines are the point of the
; `inline` golden: an inlined tier must leave every one of them where it
; is.
(timeline :title "by reference" :length 1bar)

(tempo-point :at 0q :qpm 120)
(meter-point :at 0bar :sig [4 4])

(anchor :id song :kind smf :file "../../../corpus/skeleton-smf/song.mid" :size 120 :sha256 "09163f39f8fb7392cd866030aa90dadb9445406aac5a3efef3f435cd92608d4b")

(lane :name flash :target flash
  ; the downbeat
  (note :at 0q :dur 0.5q :key 36 :vel 110))
